      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Unused imports (`CharEncoding`, `UnsupportedCharsetException`, `assertFalse`, `assertNull`, `assertEquals`)\n- Unused fields (`SWISS_GERMAN_STUFF_UNICODE`, `RUSSIAN_STUFF_UNICODE`) and unused helper method (`constructString`)\n- The array comment is cryptic (\"Require the RFC 1522 'encoded-word' header\")\n- The array is formatted as one dense line, making the cases hard to scan\n- No explanation of what makes these Base64 strings \"impossible\"\n\nLet me write the improved test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports, unused fields (`SWISS_GERMAN_STUFF_UNICODE`, `RUSSIAN_STUFF_UNICODE`), and the dead `constructString` helper, formats the `BASE64_IMPOSSIBLE_CASES` array one entry per line with inline comments explaining each case, and adds descriptive failure messages and a clarifying comment that explains why strict mode must reject these inputs."
